Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:16:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 108/110] Closing every tab of one view keeps the other view's
 tab in front

Closing a tab picked the next one by position in the tab order of both
views, so closing the last tab of a view (by Close all, the x button or
Ctrl+W) could switch the remaining view to a tab it was not showing. Now
a close that empties a view keeps the tab the other view shows; other
closes still go to the nearest neighbour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

